  "question": {
    "text": "A line passes through the point $(-1,1)$ and makes an angle $\\sin ^{-1}\\left(\\frac{3}{5}\\right)$ in the positive direction of $x$-axis. If this line meets the curve $x^2=4 y-9$ at $A$ and $B$, then $|A B|$ is equal to",
